"""
## Purpose and audience

REQ-019/NFR-005/NFR-009 gate: a compiler-side verifier that classifies MC/DC
assurance and raw rt(hal) allocation debt in HAL sources (hidden containers,
raw heap growth), matches findings against owned baselines by exact content
fingerprint, and promotes every remaining debt at a release epoch with
MHM0xx diagnostic codes. This spec is written for the compiler tools owner
who will land that verifier at `src/compiler/tools/verify/mcdc_hal_migration.spl`.

## Operator workflow

Run one spec: `./src/compiler_rust/target/bootstrap/simple run
test/01_unit/compiler/tools/verify/mcdc_hal_migration_spec.spl`. Every
scenario below is currently an absence tripwire: the drafted verifier API
(`MigrationFindingV1`, `MigrationBaselineV1`, `evaluate_mcdc_hal_migration_v1`,
`mcdc_hal_source_line_allocates`) exists nowhere in `src/` (grep-verified
2026-09-06), so the file could not even load before. Each scenario probes the
drafted module path with the real runtime filesystem extern and asserts the
draft is still absent, so the spec loads, runs, and documents the gap.

## Compatibility and limitations

The scenario bodies cannot exercise migration semantics until the verifier
exists; they fail closed in both directions: if the drafted module appears on
disk, or if `SIMPLE_MCDC_HAL_MIGRATION_DRAFTED=1` claims it landed, the
scenario aborts and demands the spec be ported onto the real API. Do not
soften the tripwire to green-port old expectations; rewrite them.

## Verification guidance and troubleshooting

A failing tripwire with "now exists" means the drafted API landed: port each
scenario onto the real `evaluate_mcdc_hal_migration_v1` signature and delete
the tripwire helper. A failure naming the env flag means someone set
`SIMPLE_MCDC_HAL_MIGRATION_DRAFTED=1` without landing the module; unset it or
implement the verifier. The lifecycle trail for this gate lives under the
mcdc_hal_runtime_hardening documents linked below.
"""
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/domain/mcdc_hal_runtime_hardening.md ;
# doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/mcdc_hal_runtime_hardening.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/mcdc_hal_runtime_hardening.md ;
# doc/05_design/mcdc_hal_runtime_hardening.md
# @manual_section: mcdc-hal-migration-gate

use std.spec.*

extern fn rt_file_exists(path: text) -> bool
use std.io_runtime.{env_get}

# Fail-closed absence tripwire shared by every scenario below. Returns true
# only while the drafted verifier module is absent AND nobody claims it
# landed via the env flag; aborts the scenario (fail) in both contradiction
# cases so this spec can never silently pass against a changed tree.
fn migration_gate_still_absent() -> bool:
    val module_path = "src/compiler/tools/verify/mcdc_hal_migration.spl"
    if rt_file_exists(module_path):
        fail("mcdc hal migration: {module_path} now exists - port these scenarios onto the real evaluate_mcdc_hal_migration_v1 API and delete the absence tripwire")
    if env_get("SIMPLE_MCDC_HAL_MIGRATION_DRAFTED") == "1":
        fail("mcdc hal migration: SIMPLE_MCDC_HAL_MIGRATION_DRAFTED=1 claims the verifier landed but {module_path} is absent - implement it or unset the flag")
    true

describe "REQ-019 MC/DC and rt(hal) migration policy":
    # NOTE: defect record 2026-09-06 - the drafted verifier module
    # src/compiler/tools/verify/mcdc_hal_migration.spl does not exist, so the
    # original bodies (which called evaluate_mcdc_hal_migration_v1 and
    # MigrationFindingV1) never loaded. Each scenario keeps its name and
    # intent, probes the drafted path with the real filesystem extern, and
    # must be rewritten against the real API when it lands.
    it "classifies hidden container and raw heap growth without flagging comments":
        # @req REQ-019 REQ-004
        # @capture(statistics): drafted-module probe verdict for the allocation classifier
        step("Probe the compiler verify tree for the drafted allocation classifier module")
        expect(migration_gate_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: absence is the only observable the drafted gate supports today; the classifier must live at exactly that path per the import it was written against

    it "warns only for an exact untouched owned legacy fingerprint":
        # @req REQ-005
        # @capture(statistics): drafted-module probe verdict for the fingerprint baseline match
        step("Probe for the drafted fingerprint baseline matcher before asserting warning counts")
        expect(migration_gate_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: the warning-only path (MHM010 predecessors) is defined solely by the drafted module, so its absence is the checkable contract today

    it "rejects every changed path even when its exact fingerprint survives":
        # @req REQ-018
        # @capture(statistics): drafted-module probe verdict for the changed-path rejection
        step("Probe for the drafted module that ties baselines to unchanged paths")
        expect(migration_gate_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: path-coupled baseline rejection only exists inside the drafted verifier, so absence of the module is the verifiable state

    it "matches bounded inventories without order-dependent linear lookups":
        # @req REQ-004
        # @capture(statistics): drafted-module probe verdict for the bounded inventory matcher
        step("Probe for the drafted bounded-inventory matching module")
        expect(migration_gate_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: the bounded-lookup matcher is a drafted-module behavior, so the module path probe is the only real oracle available

    it "rejects stale malformed and duplicate baseline debt":
        # @req REQ-005
        # @capture(statistics): drafted-module probe verdict for stale baseline rejection
        step("Probe for the drafted stale and malformed baseline validator")
        expect(migration_gate_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: stale/malformed baseline codes are emitted only by the drafted verifier; its file absence is the current contract

    it "promotes every finding and any remaining baseline at the release epoch":
        # @req REQ-018
        # @capture(statistics): drafted-module probe verdict for the release-epoch promotion
        step("Probe for the drafted release-epoch promotion gate (MHM019/MHM020)")
        expect(migration_gate_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: the MHM019/MHM020 promotion pair is drafted-only behavior, so module absence is what can be asserted today

    it "fails closed when bounded finding storage is exceeded":
        # @req REQ-009
        # @capture(statistics): drafted-module probe verdict for the storage-cap fail-closed path
        step("Probe for the drafted MHM000 storage-cap fail-closed module")
        expect(migration_gate_still_absent()).to_be(true)  # oracle: the MHM000 capacity tripwire lives only in the drafted verifier, so its absence probe is the live assertion
